{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787354432119748001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"honest-repulsive-blackfish","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"6efbb185a7fd6c258e3b2669c05d0ea800e9a74f94553b7396ccdfc45b106a2c","event_uuid":"de433202-df72-417e-b489-cefcf13be8f4","position":{"commit_sha":"b0016e96e949b687ff81d1804a446ba036fb9583","position":"1787352123041738001-de433202-df72-417e-b489-cefcf13be8f4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f0af4046d278e766842c585c5bd5d82d7adfd77f497a054f63cb535b0da735f8","event_uuid":"f0074985-e6f8-4aa5-b09b-e271b5495aa5","position":{"commit_sha":"739b60dc5eb5dc6c8b2ea93ca2749c36073256a4","position":"1787352128084121001-f0074985-e6f8-4aa5-b09b-e271b5495aa5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f31d01d35e7bff411205c87f19679cca5c9711da2de03d426fc9cc78fac20d36","event_uuid":"d96850ba-1855-40a2-8c33-6c57f2468e32","position":{"commit_sha":"82f9ebb411fd16ade683cb12f7d5249b4edca579","position":"1787352135748598001-d96850ba-1855-40a2-8c33-6c57f2468e32"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787352123041738001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d96850ba-1855-40a2-8c33-6c57f2468e32","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7bc2-5203-d5f4-4a4a"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nGit failure strings are classified at five sites with different verdicts for the same text: `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:215,221,517` (index-lock and transient-FS markers, retried locally), `src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py:48,61,110` (non-FF / policy-decline / transport markers), `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock_push.py:68,74` and `_advisory_lock.py:272` (CAS mismatch, terminal), `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:465` (invalid-object recovery). `cannot lock ref` receives three different verdicts; the synthetic `git timed out after` result is produced by three `_git` shims (`push.py:71`, `sync.py:66`, `event_commit_git.py:64`) and treated as retriable by one. Bug `unheedful-custodial-bluebottle` was two of these drifting; `wrongful-chemic-squeaker` added the transient retry to `s3_doctor` only, leaving `sync` and `push_recovery` merges without it.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `src/rebar/_store/git_outcome.py`: one marker registry and `classify(result) -> GitOutcome` with kinds `LOCK, TRANSIENT_FS, TRANSPORT, NON_FF, CAS_MISMATCH, POLICY_DECLINE, DIRTY_WD, UNMERGED, FATAL`, the subtractive \"policy wins over non-FF\" rule applied once, and `run_git(..., retry=RetryPolicy)` that folds the timeout shims. Existing predicates become lookups; marker tables move, not change. Guard test: the marker strings (`index.lock`, `non-fast-forward`, `cannot lock ref`, `could not parse head`) appear in `src/rebar` only in `git_outcome.py` (`# git-marker-ok:` escape).\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_store/git_outcome.py` (new), `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py`, `src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py`, `src/rebar/_store/push.py`, `src/rebar/_store/sync.py`, `src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py`, `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py`, `src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock_push.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_advisory_lock.py`, `tests/unit/store/test_git_outcome.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nTable-driven test: one captured stderr per kind (taken from the existing tests' fixtures) maps to exactly one kind. Edge: a stderr carrying both `rejected` and a policy-decline marker classifies POLICY_DECLINE. Pinning: `tests/unit/test_gitutil_transient_write_retry.py`, `tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py`, `tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py`, `tests/unit/test_push_rejection_surfacing.py`, `tests/unit/test_push_policy.py`, `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor*.py`, the reconciler ref-lock tests pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every current marker string resolves to one kind and the kind-to-action mapping at each caller is unchanged; checked by the table test plus the pinning suites.\n- [ ] `sync._union_merge` and `push_recovery` merges now retry TRANSIENT_FS faults through the shared `run_git`; checked by a new test injecting `could not parse head` once into a reconverge merge.\n- [ ] The guard test passes and the four `_git` timeout shims are deleted; checked by `grep -rn \"timed out after\" src/rebar/_store`.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/git_outcome.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/sync.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_commit_git.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/event_append.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock_push.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_advisory_lock.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"tests/unit/store/test_git_outcome.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a"],["relates_to","7bc2-5203-d5f4-4a4a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["consolidation","janitor","fortnight-review"],"ticket_id":"d6e3-548c-37eb-4c45","ticket_type":"story","title":"One git failure classifier and retry policy for store git operations","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["de433202-df72-417e-b489-cefcf13be8f4","f0074985-e6f8-4aa5-b09b-e271b5495aa5","d96850ba-1855-40a2-8c33-6c57f2468e32"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787354432119748001,"uuid":"e7317e9f-99b9-4059-8bf8-37778aabeea5"}